{"availability":"available","full":"maxliebscher/threejs-procedural-rocks-cliffs","name":"threejs-procedural-rocks-cliffs","description":"Watertight procedural rock fields and cliffs in Three.js, with an interactive demo and Codex skill.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":17,"forks":4,"created":"2026-09-01T21:18:17Z","updated":"2026-09-01T22:12:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://maxliebscher.github.io/threejs-procedural-rocks-cliffs/","topics":["codex-skill","marching-tetrahedra","procedural-generation","sdf","threejs","webgl"],"demo":"https://maxliebscher.github.io/threejs-procedural-rocks-cliffs/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:37:54.880Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T06:37:54.880Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T06:37:54.880Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:09:40.991Z","stars":17,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-08T06:37:54.880Z","stars":17,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive Three.js demonstrator for drawing terrain-bound rock fields and watertight cliff masses. An editable footprint becomes a deterministic geological scalar field, one connected surface, a topology audit, and a metric triplanar PBR material.","This is a focused technical demo rather than a complete terrain editor. It makes the difficult part inspectable: believable fused stone masses that remain closed, deterministic, terrain-aware, and responsive enough for interactive authoring.","Independent rock meshes intersect internally and explicit profile lofts tend to create seams, self-intersections, or cut-block silhouettes when many natural masses must fuse. This demo represents the main geological body as one continuous scalar field and extracts a single surface from the union."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maxliebscher/threejs-procedural-rocks-cliffs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"00914e9395129e127757bbeddfa0de10a9f7b5ca4102a8c9